<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>日本語 Japan Bootcamp</title>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Noto+Serif+JP:wght@400;700&family=DM+Mono:wght@400;500&family=Playfair+Display:ital,wght@0,700;1,400&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
  :root {
    --ink: #1a1008;
    --paper: #faf6ef;
    --red: #c0392b;
    --gold: #b8860b;
    --muted: #7a6a5a;
    --light: #ede8df;
    --accent: #d4522a;
  }

  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }

  body {
    font-family: 'DM Mono', monospace;
    background: var(--paper);
    color: var(--ink);
    min-height: 100vh;
  }

  /* HEADER */
  header {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
    padding: 2rem 2rem 1.5rem;
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  header::before {
    content: '日本';
    position: absolute;
    right: -1rem;
    top: -1rem;
    font-family: 'Noto Serif JP', serif;
    font-size: 8rem;
    color: rgba(255,255,255,0.04);
    line-height: 1;
  }
  header h1 {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.1;
  }
  header h1 span { color: var(--accent); font-style: italic; }
  header p {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    color: rgba(250,246,239,0.55);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  /* NAV TABS */
  nav {
    display: flex;
    background: var(--ink);
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);
    overflow-x: auto;
    scrollbar-width: none;
  }
  nav::-webkit-scrollbar { display: none; }
  nav button {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.4rem;
    background: none;
    border: none;
    color: rgba(250,246,239,0.45);
    font-family: 'DM Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    cursor: pointer;
    border-bottom: 2px solid transparent;
    transition: all 0.2s;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  nav button:hover { color: var(--paper); }
  nav button.active { color: var(--accent); border-bottom-color: var(--accent); }

  /* MAIN */
  main { padding: 1.5rem 1.2rem 4rem; max-width: 680px; margin: 0 auto; }

  /* SECTION PANELS */
  .panel { display: none; animation: fadeUp 0.3s ease; }
  .panel.active { display: block; }
  @keyframes fadeUp {
    from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(8px); }
    to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
  }

  /* CATEGORY LABEL */
  .cat-label {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.7rem;
    margin: 1.8rem 0 0.8rem;
  }
  .cat-label span.jp {
    font-family: 'Noto Serif JP', serif;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .cat-label span.en {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--muted);
    padding-top: 2px;
    flex: 1;
  }

  /* PHRASE CARDS */
  .phrase-card {
    background: white;
    border: 1px solid var(--light);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: all 0.15s;
    position: relative;
  }
  .phrase-card:hover { border-color: var(--accent); transform: translateX(2px); }
  .phrase-card .jp-text {
    font-family: 'Noto Serif JP', serif;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    line-height: 1.4;
  }
  .phrase-card .romaji {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-top: 0.2rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }
  .phrase-card .meaning {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-top: 0.15rem;
  }
  .phrase-card .tip {
    display: none;
    margin-top: 0.7rem;
    padding-top: 0.7rem;
    border-top: 1px dashed var(--light);
    font-size: 0.73rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .phrase-card.open .tip { display: block; }
  .phrase-card .toggle-hint {
    position: absolute;
    top: 1rem; right: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    color: var(--light);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }
  .phrase-card:hover .toggle-hint { color: var(--muted); }

  /* BOOTCAMP */
  .week-header {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 1rem 1.2rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0.6rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .week-header .week-num {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
    font-size: 2rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .week-header .week-info { flex: 1; }
  .week-header .week-title {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .week-header .week-goal {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    color: rgba(250,246,239,0.5);
    margin-top: 0.2rem;
  }

  .day-card {
    background: white;
    border: 1px solid var(--light);
    border-radius: 6px;
    margin-bottom: 0.45rem;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .day-card-header {
    padding: 0.8rem 1rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.8rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background 0.15s;
  }
  .day-card-header:hover { background: var(--light); }
  .day-num {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 700;
    min-width: 2.5rem;
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .day-title { font-size: 0.78rem; letter-spacing: 0.04em; }
  .day-subtitle { font-size: 0.68rem; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 0.1rem; }
  .day-badge {
    margin-left: auto;
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    background: var(--light);
    color: var(--muted);
    padding: 0.2rem 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 20px;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .day-body {
    display: none;
    padding: 0 1rem 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--light);
  }
  .day-card.open .day-body { display: block; }
  .day-body ul {
    list-style: none;
    margin-top: 0.7rem;
  }
  .day-body ul li {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
    padding-left: 1rem;
    position: relative;
  }
  .day-body ul li::before {
    content: '—';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .day-body .focus-phrase {
    margin-top: 0.8rem;
    background: var(--light);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 0.6rem 0.8rem;
  }
  .day-body .focus-phrase .label {
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .day-body .focus-phrase .jp {
    font-family: 'Noto Serif JP', serif;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-top: 0.1rem;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .day-body .focus-phrase .rom {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  /* TIPS PAGE */
  .tip-block {
    background: white;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0;
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
  }
  .tip-block h3 {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
  .tip-block p, .tip-block li {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .tip-block ul { list-style: none; padding-left: 0.5rem; }
  .tip-block ul li::before { content: '· '; color: var(--accent); }

  /* QUIZ */
  .quiz-box {
    background: white;
    border: 1px solid var(--light);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .quiz-box .q-jp {
    font-family: 'Noto Serif JP', serif;
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
  .quiz-box .q-hint {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
  }
  .quiz-options {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .quiz-options button {
    padding: 0.7rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--light);
    border-radius: 5px;
    background: var(--paper);
    font-family: 'DM Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: all 0.15s;
  }
  .quiz-options button:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }
  .quiz-options button.correct { background: #e8f5e9; border-color: #4caf50; color: #2e7d32; }
  .quiz-options button.wrong { background: #ffebee; border-color: #ef9a9a; color: #c62828; }
  #quiz-result {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    min-height: 1.5em;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  #quiz-next {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    padding: 0.6rem 1.5rem;
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
    border: none;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-family: 'DM Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    cursor: pointer;
    display: none;
  }
  #quiz-next:hover { background: var(--accent); }
  .score-bar {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 0.6rem 0;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .score-bar strong { color: var(--accent); font-size: 1rem; }

  .section-intro {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    padding: 0.8rem 1rem;
    background: white;
    border-radius: 6px;
    border: 1px solid var(--light);
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<header>
  <h1>Japan <span>Survival</span><br>Phrasebook</h1>
  <p>3-week bootcamp · Restaurant to daily life</p>
</header>

<nav>
  <button class="active" onclick="showPanel('phrases')">Phrases</button>
  <button onclick="showPanel('bootcamp')">Bootcamp</button>
  <button onclick="showPanel('quiz')">Quiz</button>
  <button onclick="showPanel('tips')">Tips</button>
</nav>

<main>

<!-- ===== PHRASES ===== -->
<div class="panel active" id="panel-phrases">
  <div class="section-intro">Tap any phrase to reveal usage tips. The romaji is your pronunciation guide — read it like English.</div>

  <!-- RESTAURANT -->
  <div class="cat-label"><span class="jp">食堂</span><span class="en">Restaurant & Food</span></div>

  <div class="phrase-card" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
    <span class="toggle-hint">tap</span>
    <div class="jp-text">これをください</div>
    <div class="romaji">Kore wo kudasai</div>
    <div class="meaning">I'll have this one, please</div>
    <div class="tip">🍱 Point at the menu item or plastic food display while saying this. Works in any restaurant — no other words needed.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="phrase-card" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
    <span class="toggle-hint">tap</span>
    <div class="jp-text">二人です</div>
    <div class="romaji">Futari desu</div>
    <div class="meaning">Table for two</div>
    <div class="tip">👥 Hold up two fingers as you say it. For other numbers: hitori (1), sannin (3), yonin (4). The host will usually understand fingers alone.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="phrase-card" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
    <span class="toggle-hint">tap</span>
    <div class="jp-text">ありがとうございます</div>
    <div class="romaji">Arigatō gozaimasu</div>
    <div class="meaning">Thank you (polite)</div>
    <div class="tip">🙏 The full polite form. A slight bow adds warmth. Casual "arigatō" works between peers, but in shops and restaurants use the full version.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="phrase-card" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
    <span class="toggle-hint">tap</span>
    <div class="jp-text">すみません</div>
    <div class="romaji">Sumimasen</div>
    <div class="meaning">Excuse me / Sorry (to get attention)</div>
    <div class="tip">🙋 Your most-used word. Call a waiter, squeeze past someone, interrupt someone — this covers all of it. Say it with a slight bow.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="phrase-card" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
    <span class="toggle-hint">tap</span>
    <div class="jp-text">お会計をお願いします</div>
    <div class="romaji">Okaikei wo onegaishimasu</div>
    <div class="meaning">The bill, please</div>
    <div class="tip">💴 Or mime writing on your palm — staff will understand. Many restaurants have a ticket machine at the door instead of table billing.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="phrase-card" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
    <span class="toggle-hint">tap</span>
    <div class="jp-text">おいしい！</div>
    <div class="romaji">Oishii!</div>
    <div class="meaning">Delicious!</div>
    <div class="tip">😋 Japanese chefs and hosts genuinely appreciate this. Say it after your first bite and they'll love you.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="phrase-card" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
    <span class="toggle-hint">tap</span>
    <div class="jp-text">水をください</div>
    <div class="romaji">Mizu wo kudasai</div>
    <div class="meaning">Water, please</div>
    <div class="tip">💧 Water is almost always free in Japan. Tap water is perfectly safe and clean everywhere.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="phrase-card" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
    <span class="toggle-hint">tap</span>
    <div class="jp-text">アレルギーがあります</div>
    <div class="romaji">Arerugī ga arimasu</div>
    <div class="meaning">I have an allergy</div>
    <div class="tip">⚠️ Follow with the food: "ebi" (shrimp), "nattsu" (nuts), "guruten" (gluten). Consider carrying an allergy card in Japanese — restaurants take this very seriously.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="phrase-card" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
    <span class="toggle-hint">tap</span>
    <div class="jp-text">おすすめは何ですか？</div>
    <div class="romaji">Osusume wa nan desu ka?</div>
    <div class="meaning">What do you recommend?</div>
    <div class="tip">⭐ Staff will be delighted you asked. Point to what they suggest and say "kore wo kudasai."</div>
  </div>

  <div class="phrase-card" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
    <span class="toggle-hint">tap</span>
    <div class="jp-text">いただきます</div>
    <div class="romaji">Itadakimasu</div>
    <div class="meaning">Let's eat (said before eating)</div>
    <div class="tip">🥢 Said before a meal, hands together. There's no direct English translation — it's gratitude for the food and everyone involved in making it.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="phrase-card" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
    <span class="toggle-hint">tap</span>
    <div class="jp-text">ごちそうさまでした</div>
    <div class="romaji">Gochisōsama deshita</div>
    <div class="meaning">Thank you for the meal (after eating)</div>
    <div class="tip">🙏 Said when leaving a restaurant. Staff will bow and appreciate it enormously. Makes you instantly likeable.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="phrase-card" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
    <span class="toggle-hint">tap</span>
    <div class="jp-text">持ち帰りで</div>
    <div class="romaji">Mochikaeri de</div>
    <div class="meaning">To take away</div>
    <div class="tip">📦 For eat-in say "koko de" instead. At convenience stores (konbini), you can just point to the item.</div>
  </div>

  <!-- GREETINGS -->
  <div class="cat-label"><span class="jp">挨拶</span><span class="en">Greetings & Politeness</span></div>

  <div class="phrase-card" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
    <span class="toggle-hint">tap</span>
    <div class="jp-text">こんにちは</div>
    <div class="romaji">Konnichiwa</div>
    <div class="meaning">Hello / Good afternoon</div>
    <div class="tip">☀️ Used from midday to early evening. Morning: "ohayō gozaimasu." Evening: "konbanwa."</div>
  </div>

  <div class="phrase-card" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
    <span class="toggle-hint">tap</span>
    <div class="jp-text">おはようございます</div>
    <div class="romaji">Ohayō gozaimasu</div>
    <div class="meaning">Good morning</div>
    <div class="tip">🌅 Used until about 11am. Drop the "gozaimasu" with people your own age in casual settings.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="phrase-card" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
    <span class="toggle-hint">tap</span>
    <div class="jp-text">はい / いいえ</div>
    <div class="romaji">Hai / Iie</div>
    <div class="meaning">Yes / No</div>
    <div class="tip">✅ "Hai" also means "okay" or "understood." Japanese people often avoid a direct "iie" — watch for hesitation or "chotto..." (a little difficult) which usually means no.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="phrase-card" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
    <span class="toggle-hint">tap</span>
    <div class="jp-text">わかりません</div>
    <div class="romaji">Wakarimasen</div>
    <div class="meaning">I don't understand</div>
    <div class="tip">🤷 Smile when you say it. Staff will often switch to gestures or show you a phone translator.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="phrase-card" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
    <span class="toggle-hint">tap</span>
    <div class="jp-text">英語を話せますか？</div>
    <div class="romaji">Eigo wo hanasemasu ka?</div>
    <div class="meaning">Do you speak English?</div>
    <div class="tip">💬 Many younger people in cities have some English. In rural areas, Google Translate camera mode is your best friend.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="phrase-card" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
    <span class="toggle-hint">tap</span>
    <div class="jp-text">もう一度お願いします</div>
    <div class="romaji">Mō ichido onegaishimasu</div>
    <div class="meaning">Please say that again</div>
    <div class="tip">🔁 Also works with a gesture — rotate your hand as if winding something. Staff are patient and helpful.</div>
  </div>

  <!-- SHOPPING -->
  <div class="cat-label"><span class="jp">買い物</span><span class="en">Shopping & Money</span></div>

  <div class="phrase-card" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
    <span class="toggle-hint">tap</span>
    <div class="jp-text">いくらですか？</div>
    <div class="romaji">Ikura desu ka?</div>
    <div class="meaning">How much is this?</div>
    <div class="tip">💰 Shopkeepers may show you a calculator with the number. Japan is largely cash-based — always carry yen. Post office ATMs (JP Bank) reliably accept foreign cards.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="phrase-card" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
    <span class="toggle-hint">tap</span>
    <div class="jp-text">カードで払えますか？</div>
    <div class="romaji">Kādo de haraemasu ka?</div>
    <div class="meaning">Can I pay by card?</div>
    <div class="tip">💳 Many small restaurants and shops are cash-only. Look for card symbols on the door, or ask before ordering.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="phrase-card" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
    <span class="toggle-hint">tap</span>
    <div class="jp-text">袋はいりません</div>
    <div class="romaji">Fukuro wa irimasen</div>
    <div class="meaning">No bag needed, thanks</div>
    <div class="tip">🛍️ Japan charges for plastic bags. Saying this saves money and shows eco-awareness — staff appreciate it.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="phrase-card" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
    <span class="toggle-hint">tap</span>
    <div class="jp-text">見ているだけです</div>
    <div class="romaji">Mite iru dake desu</div>
    <div class="meaning">I'm just looking</div>
    <div class="tip">👀 Staff in Japan are attentive and will often greet you and offer help. This is a polite way to browse freely.</div>
  </div>

  <!-- TRANSPORT -->
  <div class="cat-label"><span class="jp">交通</span><span class="en">Transport & Navigation</span></div>

  <div class="phrase-card" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
    <span class="toggle-hint">tap</span>
    <div class="jp-text">〜はどこですか？</div>
    <div class="romaji">~ wa doko desu ka?</div>
    <div class="meaning">Where is [place]?</div>
    <div class="tip">🗺️ Replace ~ with the place name. E.g. "Toire wa doko desu ka?" = Where is the toilet? Show the kanji/name on your phone for place names.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="phrase-card" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
    <span class="toggle-hint">tap</span>
    <div class="jp-text">〜に行きたいです</div>
    <div class="romaji">~ ni ikitai desu</div>
    <div class="meaning">I want to go to [place]</div>
    <div class="tip">🚉 For taxis, just show the destination on your phone. Most taxi drivers won't speak English but navigate by GPS.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="phrase-card" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
    <span class="toggle-hint">tap</span>
    <div class="jp-text">右 / 左 / まっすぐ</div>
    <div class="romaji">Migi / Hidari / Massugu</div>
    <div class="meaning">Right / Left / Straight ahead</div>
    <div class="tip">↔️ Essential for giving or following directions. Gesture as you say them — people will understand immediately.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="phrase-card" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
    <span class="toggle-hint">tap</span>
    <div class="jp-text">〜番線はどこですか？</div>
    <div class="romaji">~ bansen wa doko desu ka?</div>
    <div class="meaning">Where is platform [number]?</div>
    <div class="tip">🚆 Japanese train stations are well-signposted in English, but this helps in older rural stations. IC card (Suica/Pasmo) removes most ticketing stress.</div>
  </div>

  <!-- EMERGENCIES -->
  <div class="cat-label"><span class="jp">緊急</span><span class="en">Emergencies</span></div>

  <div class="phrase-card" onclick="toggleCard(this)">
    <span class="toggle-hint">tap</span>
